{
  "baseline_commit": "e8cc9648",
  "kernel_recipe_revision": "f333bc9fec9ce7843fb407f00d0ece5c",
  "protocol": [
    "Linux release, serial Worker groups. Each stored fixture reuses the same accepted predecessor, bypasses the final artifact hit, and executes one tip feature per sample. Elapsed is service preview wall time; Worker stages are nested.",
    "For the existing 500/1000 fixtures, both comparison arms use a test overlay holding the predecessor evaluator generation fixed. Production uses the new kernel generation for the current key and checkpoint admission. Separate fresh 120-step and STEP tests exercise production keys.",
    "First sample on each fresh worker has no face seed. Subsequent samples edit the same tip using different heights. RSS is process high-water bytes. Service visual bytes include the complete visual representation. Worker GLB bytes describe the encoded mesh.",
    "Independent native index trace, outside timed runs: two indexed faces of 2504 entries per 1000-step tip operation. Entry counts do not measure allocator bytes. The native kernel RSS and cancel time are one observation per binary.",
    "STEP first cut is one sample per binary on independently imported 456-face generated inputs. The production Router also checks depth change, material removal, preview promotion and cold replay."
  ],
